{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\niv=[x for x in s['interpretations'] if x['id'].startswith('7e17be3e')][0]\nprint(iv['rationale'])\nprint('---COUNTER')\nfor c in iv['counterevidence']: print('-',c)\nprint('---LIMITS')\nfor c in iv['limitations']: print('-',c)\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\niv=[x for x in s['interpretations'] if x['id'].startswith('7e17be3e')][0]\nprint(iv['rationale'])\nprint('---COUNTER')\nfor c in iv['counterevidence']: print('-',c)\nprint('---LIMITS')\nfor c in iv['limitations']: print('-',c)\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"The suspicion is refuted for the captured legal paths, although the low-level code alone would count it. handleLeaderHeartbeatResp confirms when a heartbeat response carries a nonzero hint, lw admits observer responses, and readIndex.confirm counts the responding node without checking whether it is currently a voter. That is the plausible weakness. The legal transition path does not create the needed state: membership rejects AddObserver or AddWitness for a current address; RemoveNode deletes the node from remotes, observers, and witnesses and marks it removed; isAddRemovedNode rejects re-adding that ID as any role; and raft.restore panics if a non-observer or non-witness local node appears in the snapshot's observer or witness set. In addition, broadcastHeartbeatMessageWithHint sends nonzero-context heartbeats only to votingMembers and sends observer heartbeats only for the zero context. A delayed response from a removed voter is therefore ignored because lw no longer finds it in any role map, and a delayed nonzero context cannot come from an observer under legal transitions. The rejoining-as-observer path is blocked by membership. The conclusion is a protective-mechanism negative result, not a claim that arbitrary direct map mutation or a malicious observer is safe; those are outside the admitted scenario and would still expose the low-level counting behavior.\n---COUNTER\n- The low-level path does not check voter eligibility in readIndex.confirm; it counts any nonzero-hint response that lw admits.\n- Observers are admitted by lw for heartbeat responses and are not filtered out by readIndex.confirm.\n- The refutation depends on the legal membership guards and nonzero-hint routing, not on the absence of these low-level behaviors.\n---LIMITS\n- Direct mutation of the raft role maps, an operator restarting a node with a role inconsistent with cluster membership, forged heartbeat responses, or a custom transport that changes admission are excluded.\n- This source-only account does not run an execution; it relies on the captured membership and raft control flow.\n- The established main finding remains separate: a legal follower-originated ReadIndex batch can receive another request's context and fail to complete.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\niv=[x for x in s['interpretations'] if x['id'].startswith('7e17be3e')][0]\nout={k:iv[k] for k in ('investigation_id','experiment_id','source_ids','executions','conclusion','defect_claim','rationale','answers','knowledge','counterevidence','limitations','joint_history')}\nout['executions']={\\\"ec7794827f40455b8a20ef667e3b7461\\\":[1,2,3]}\nmarker=\\\"The rejoining-as-observer path is blocked by membership.\\\"\nadd=(\\\" The admission layers are now measured as well: with one read queued at a leader for voters {1,2,3}, a confirming heartbeat response from node 4, which sits in no role map, left the queue unchanged both when delivered through the Peer and when handed straight to the raft state machine, \\\"\n     \\\"while the same response from voter 3 confirmed the context and produced a reply for the requester.\\\")\nassert marker in out['rationale']\nout['rationale']=out['rationale'].replace(marker, marker+add)\nout['knowledge'].append({\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"@unknown-sender-cannot-confirm-readindex\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\n \\\"assertion\\\":\\\"A response from a sender outside every role map left the pending read unconfirmed at both admission layers, while a current voter's response confirmed it.\\\"})\nout['counterevidence'].append(\\\"Both admission layers reject an unadmitted sender in the measured execution, so the counting behavior in readIndex.confirm is only reachable for a sender one of those layers admits.\\\")\nout['limitations'][1]=(\\\"The execution starts from post-transition role maps directly and does not run a live configuration change; it covers an unknown sender, not a specifically removed voter whose maps were updated by an applied removal.\\\")\nfact={\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@unknown-sender-cannot-confirm-readindex\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":(\\\"In the admission execution, a leader for voters {1,2,3} had one ReadIndex request queued under context {101,1002}. A HeartbeatResp carrying that context from node 4, which is in no role map, left the pending queue at its previous length and produced no replies both when delivered through the Peer admission path and when handed directly to the raft state machine; \\\"\n   \\\"the same response from voter 3 then emptied the queue and produced one ReadIndex reply addressed to the requesting node.\\\"),\n \\\"conditions\\\":(\\\"A real raft state machine built by the package test helper with committed membership {1,2,3} and a committed current-term no-op; node 4 absent from remotes, observers and witnesses; the response carries the queued context in Hint and HintHigh with a zero term; production code unchanged.\\\"),\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"peer-response-filter\\\",\\\"lw-remote-lookup\\\",\\\"leader-heartbeat-resp\\\",\\\"readindex-confirm\\\",\\\"leader-readindex-admission\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"ec7794827f40455b8a20ef667e3b7461\\\":[1,2,3]}}\njson.dump({\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Record the retained admission receipt, which turns the former-voter quorum refutation from a source trace into a measurement. The low-level counting behavior is unchanged and still documented, but a confirming heartbeat response from a sender outside every role map left a queued read unconfirmed at both the Peer and the raft layers, \\\"\n  \\\"while a current voter's response confirmed it. Add the fact, cite the receipt in the interpretation, and replace the claim that the account is source-only with the accurate scope of the execution.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[fact],\\\"interpretations\\\":[out]}, open('draft/update.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nopen('draft/update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -12\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
